Hi,

I want to say:

if (1 or 2 or 3) do (x)

However, 1, 2, and 3 have some missing data, so I get the 'missing value
where logical needed' error message.  To get around that, I wrote:

if((!is.na(1)

I received several suggestions, all of which worked nicely:

if(any(1,2,3,na.rm=T))

is.true <- function(x) return(x & !is.na(x))
if(any(is.true(c(1,2,3))))

pmax(1,2,3,na.rm=T)

Thanks to Sam Buttrey
